# Tag 1.2.5 (quay, 2026-06-03): numpy 2.3.5, pandas 2.3.3, pyarrow 24.0.0, polars 1.41.2.
#
# NOT 1.4.0. That image has NO pyarrow, and its pandas is 3.0.5 -- so nothing in it can
# read or write a parquet file, by either route. `gpr_4lane` dies on `import pyarrow`
# after all four annotation lanes have already succeeded, which is the expensive half of
# the run; Nextflow then ignores the process that exhausted its retries and the workflow
# reports `completed` with no table. Measured in both images on fir before changing this.
#
# NOT sha256:334b01e4... either -- that is what the env migration pinned, and it resolves
# to tags `1.3.1` / `plotly_no_chrome` built 2025-12-16: an OLDER image than 1.2.5 despite
# the higher version number, and one with no polars at all.
#
# The rule this file keeps relearning: a bare tag bump here is a silent dependency
# rewrite for every transform that names this env. Verify the imports in the image.
container: docker://quay.io/hallamlab/python_for_data_science:1.2.5
conda: python_for_data_science
